{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014RjSo5UyyjeZchaiQrgr9v","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief — 2026-10-06\n2\t\n3\t## The use case (two sentences, from the scout)\n4\t\n5\tEvery Saturday a free, timed, volunteer-run 5k (parkrun, in 20+ countries)\n6\tgets the same numbers: finishers, new PBs, first timers, visitors, volunteers\n7\tand the milestone clubs reached. The run director or report writer turns them\n8\tinto \"this week at our event\" for the Facebook page and the results/news\n9\tpage, today by hand in PowerPoint\n10\t([ear1grey/parkrun-event-summary](https://github.com/ear1grey/parkrun-event-summary):\n11\t\"quite cumbersome\") or as plain text\n12\t([eventuate](https://github.com/johnsyweb/eventuate),\n13\t[parkrun-runstats](https://github.com/rwkura/parkrun-milestones)).\n14\t\n15\t## Neighbours read\n16\t\n17\tPlan call 1 ran four readers and was cut off. The three digests that finished\n18\tare in [`plan-notes/`](plan-notes/): docs, neighbours, official shapes. The\n19\tparkrun facts reader did not finish, so the domain facts below come from the\n20\tscout.\n21\t\n22\t- `community/qsl-card/v1`: a fixed 6-cell table that reflows by aspect, with a\n23\t  pure layout function placed by `placeInsetPieces`. Reflowing comes first and\n24\t  shrinking is the second resort. Its lesson: chrome you cannot remove\n25\t  (`ADIF QSO CARD`) is a defect.\n26\t- `music/radio-top-30-chart/v1`: the `w*10 >= h*13` wide switch and invented\n27\t  sample data labelled in the footer. Its lesson: about 30 tile and text\n28\t  layers tripped `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP`, and the dim ink was invisible in a feed.\n29\t- `sports/cubing-average-card/v1` and `sports/swim-time-drop-card/v1`: in\n30\t  portrait, extra height turned into dead air. Tiles capped against becoming\n31\t  slabs left half a square empty.\n32\t- Official `hero/ffmpeg-pulse/kpi-overview/v1` and `github/year-card/v1`: a KPI\n33\t  grid of 4x2 / 3 / 2 columns by aspect, each tile a big number over a small\n34\t  label (value about 0.42-0.5 of tile height, label about 0.16-0.2).\n35\t\n36\tWhat is new against those: no card on the shelf is a group's week. This one\n37\thas a hierarchy across tiles (two headline numbers over four supporting ones)\n38\tand a variable badge row (0 to 10 milestone clubs) that needs an empty-week\n39\trule.\n40\t\n41\t## The template\n42\t\n43\t- id: `@one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1`. The pack exists: \"Cards a\n44\t  hobby community makes for its own members, filled from the records the hobby\n45\t  already keeps\". A weekly card made by event volunteers from the results page\n46\t  fits it word for word. `sports` holds only one athlete's PB cards.\n47\t- title: Weekly 5k Run Report\n48\t- kind: image (still PNG). Canvas hint 1080x1080 (the Facebook feed square).\n49\t  It must also work at 1920x1080 (results page, slide), 1080x1920 (story) and\n50\t  the seven contract canvases, down to 480x270, with no refusal at defaults.\n51\t- duration: still (`outputHints` `{ width: 1080, height: 1080, fps: 30,\n52\t  durationMs: 2000, format: { kind: \"image\", container: \"png\" }, note }`)\n53\t\n54\t## The design decisions\n55\t\n56\t1. **Two headline numbers, not six equal ones.** Finishers and volunteers get\n57\t   the two big tiles, side by side and the same size. An event has no run\n58\t   without either, and the run report thanks both. New PBs, first timers,\n59\t   visitors and first-time volunteers sit under them as four smaller tiles.\n60\t   Six equal tiles is variant b, so the critic can compare.\n61\t2. **Numbers are props, never fetched, never computed.** The card prints what\n62\t   the RD types. It derives no percentages, no \"record week\" and no ranking.\n63\t   The only computation is formatting (thousands comma) and the weekday from\n64\t   the date.\n65\t3. **The milestone band never moves.** With no milestones, the band stays and\n66\t   holds one line, \"No milestone clubs this week\". The card keeps the same\n67\t   shape every Saturday, which matters for a weekly series. More than 5 clubs\n68\t   wrap to two rows inside the same band.\n69\t4. **No parkrun marks.** The title, the defaults and the labels never use the\n70\t   word \"parkrun\", a logo, or the purple/apricot palette. The user's own\n71\t   `eventName` may say \"Rushmoor parkrun\"; that is their copy. Labels use\n72\t   plain words: \"finishers\", \"volunteers\", \"first timers\".\n73\t5. **Labels are fixed copy, broken in advance.** \"first-time volunteers\" is\n74\t   the long label and sets the tile label size. It is written as two lines,\n75\t   `first-time` / `volunteers`, so a 4-wide row fits at 480x270. All tile\n76\t   labels share one size (the minimum across tiles), as qsl-card does.\n77\t6. **Any mark is a prop.** The only free line is `footer`, and `\"\"` removes\n78\t   it. The template prints no credit and no pitch of its own.\n79\t\n80\t## Layout\n81\t\n82\tMargin `m = 0.05 * S`, gap `0.025 * S`, with `S = min(H, 0.75 * W)`. Bands\n83\tare fractions of the content height, given as targets, not pins. The wide\n84\tswitch is `W * 10 >= H * 13`, as in the radio and cubing cards. Place every\n85\tregion as a real rect with `placeInsetPieces` from a pure layout function, the\n86\tqsl-card shape. There are no full-canvas sources and no `size` exprs. Text is\n87\tstatic svg text in the bundled font, over a `makeColorTile` where there is a\n88\tfill. The page colour goes in `document.backgroundColor`.\n89\t\n90\tSquare and portrait (stacked), at 1080x1080:\n91\t\n92\t```\n93\t+--------------------------------------------+\n94\t| WILLOWMERE PARK 5K                         |  header ~15%\n95\t| #312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026                   |\n96\t+---------------------+----------------------+\n97\t|        214          |         31           |  hero row ~28%\n98\t|     finishers       |      volunteers      |  (2 equal tiles)\n99\t+----------+----------+----------+-----------+\n100\t|   38     |   27     |   19     |    4      |  stat row ~20%\n101\t| new PBs  | first    | visitors | first-time|  (4 equal tiles;\n102\t|          | timers   |          | volunteers|   2x2 when portrait)\n103\t+----------+----------+----------+-----------+\n104\t| MILESTONE CLUBS                            |  milestone band ~25%\n105\t|  [25] [50] [100] [25]                      |\n106\t|  4 runners 3 runners 1 runner 2 volunteers |\n107\t+--------------------------------------------+\n108\t| Sample week: event and numbers are invented|  footer ~5%\n109\t+--------------------------------------------+\n110\t```\n111\t\n112\t- Square (`0.8 <= W/H < 1.3`) puts the four stat tiles in one 4x1 row.\n113\t- Portrait (`W/H < 0.8`) makes the stat grid 2x2, and the bands grow with H\n114\t  (hero about 26%, stats about 26%). Values are capped by width as well as\n115\t  height, so 1080x1920 gets bigger numbers instead of dead air. Cap tile\n116\t  heights so a tile is never taller than about 1.3x its width. Put the slack\n117\t  between bands as equal gaps, not under the footer.\n118\t\n119\tWide (`W * 10 >= H * 13`), at 1920x1080:\n120\t\n121\t```\n122\t+------------------------------------------------------------+\n123\t| WILLOWMERE PARK 5K                 #312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026 |  header ~16%\n124\t+-------------------+----------------------------------------+\n125\t|       214         |    38 new PBs     |   27 first timers   |\n126\t|    finishers      |-------------------+---------------------|  middle ~52%\n127\t|-------------------|    19 visitors    |  4 first-time vols  |\n128\t|        31         |                   |  (two lines)        |\n129\t|    volunteers     |                   |                     |\n130\t+-------------------+-------------------+---------------------+\n131\t| MILESTONE CLUBS  [25] [50] [100] [25]                       |  band ~24%\n132\t| Sample week: event and numbers are invented                 |  footer ~5%\n133\t+------------------------------------------------------------+\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\t- The left column is about 36% of the width and holds the two hero tiles\n137\t  stacked. The right is a 2x2 stat grid.\n138\t- The run number and date move to the right end of the header line. If the\n139\t  line does not fit, they drop to a second line, the same as square.\n140\t\n141\tMilestone badges:\n142\t\n143\t- A badge is a rounded tile (`roundedRectMask`, or the `effects.rounding` of\n144\t  `makeColorTile`) with the club number big and a caption below:\n145\t  `4 runners` / `1 runner` / `2 volunteers` / `1 volunteer`.\n146\t- Run clubs fill with the accent. Volunteer clubs fill with a neutral\n147\t  (light: a tinted grey; ink flips with `onColor`), so the two kinds differ by\n148\t  fill AND by caption word, never by colour alone.\n149\t- Order: run clubs ascending, then volunteer clubs ascending.\n150\t- All badges are the same size. At most 5 per row: 6-10 badges make two rows\n151\t  of `ceil(n/2)` and `floor(n/2)`. A row narrower than the band is centred.\n152\t\n153\tOverlay depth: about 6 tiles x 3 layers, 10 badges x 3 and the header and\n154\tfooter come to near 50 sources. Keep each text in its own tile's cell, as a\n155\t2-layer stack (fill plus text), never a full-canvas chain. Check the CLI for\n156\t`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` at 10 badges, and use child documents per band if it\n157\tfires (the powerlifting fix).\n158\t\n159\t## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps)\n160\t\n161\tLabels are the build's to name; these are the promises.\n162\t\n163\t- Every text fits its box (`textFitsMeasured`, budget `cell * 0.94 - 2px`).\n164\t  That covers event name, run line, each value, each label line, the band\n165\t  title, each badge number and caption, the empty-week line and the footer.\n166\t  Use one label per field and tile, since the copy differs.\n167\t- Header at the top: event name `within yFrac [0, 0.25]`.\n168\t- Footer at the bottom when present: `within yFrac [0.9, 1]`.\n169\t- Hero tiles: exactly 2, `equal: \"size\"` (tolerancePx 2), each\n170\t  `within yFrac [0.1, 0.8]`.\n171\t- Stat tiles: exactly 4, `equal: \"size\"` (tolerancePx 2), each\n172\t  `minWidthFrac 0.15`.\n173\t- Milestone band: `within yFrac [0.55, 1]`, `minWidthFrac 0.85`. It is\n174\t  present every week. Badges are `equal: \"size\"` when there are 2 or more,\n175\t  each `within` the band's y range. With 0 badges the contract declares the\n176\t  empty-week line instead of the badge label, so there is no `missing-label`\n177\t  and no `too-few`.\n178\t- Presence: a value and a label for all six counts; one badge per milestone\n179\t  entry.\n180\t- No pinned fractions. The use case does not ask for one.\n181\t\n182\tIn the test, not the contract:\n183\t\n184\t- The hero value px is at least 1.5x the stat value px, at every contract\n185\t  canvas.\n186\t- All tile labels share one px size.\n187\t- Badge order and captions are as listed in the test vectors.\n188\t- Determinism, and each validation error by message.\n189\t- A grep over the defaults and labels finds no \"parkrun\".\n190\t\n191\t## Props (name · type · default · what it changes · required?)\n192\t\n193\t| # | prop | type | default | what it changes |\n194\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n195\t| 1 | `eventName` | string | `\"Willowmere Park 5k\"` | Header title, drawn in caps. Up to 40 characters. |\n196\t| 2 | `runNumber` | number | `312` | `#312` in the run line. Integer 1-9999. |\n197\t| 3 | `date` | string | `\"2026-10-03\"` | `SAT 03 OCT 2026` in the run line. `\"\"` drops the date and its separator. |\n198\t| 4 | `counts` | json | `{\"finishers\":214,\"newPbs\":38,\"firstTimers\":27,\"visitors\":19,\"volunteers\":31,\"firstTimeVolunteers\":4}` | The six tiles. |\n199\t| 5 | `milestones` | string | `\"4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25\"` | The badges. `\"\"` shows the empty-week line. |\n200\t| 6 | `footer` | string | `\"Sample week: event and numbers are invented\"` | The bottom line. `\"\"` removes it, and the slack goes to the gaps. |\n201\t| 7 | `accent` | string (colour) | `\"#1f7a4d\"` | Run-club badge fill, the header rule and the hero numbers. |\n202\t| 8 | `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | Draws the layout-intent overlay. |\n203\t\n204\tAll props are optional and every default renders a full card.\n205\t\n206\tRules, not props:\n207\t\n208\t- **`counts`**:\n209\t  - It must hold exactly the six keys above, each an integer >= 0.\n210\t    `finishers` must be >= 1.\n211\t  - An unknown key is refused by name (\"counts: unknown key 'pb'; use\n212\t    finishers, newPbs, ...\"), because a silently ignored key is the QSL lesson.\n213\t  - A missing key is refused by name. An invented default never fills a real\n214\t    week.\n215\t  - Sanity checks:\n216\t    - `newPbs`, `firstTimers` and `visitors` are each <= `finishers`.\n217\t    - `firstTimeVolunteers` <= `volunteers`.\n218\t    - Values go up to 9999.\n219\t  - Each field is bound with `bindPropPath(cell, \"counts\", [key], \"number\")`.\n220\t- **Number format**: a thousands comma from 1000 up (`1204` -> `1,204`). Use\n221\t  ASCII digits, and no \"k\" abbreviation; the RD wants the exact count.\n222\t- **`milestones`**:\n223\t  - Comma-separated entries `<count>x<R|V><club>`, case-insensitive, with\n224\t    whitespace tolerated. This is the\n225\t    [parkrun-runstats](https://github.com/rwkura/parkrun-milestones) line\n226\t    (`4xR25, 4xR50, 1xR100`) plus `V` for volunteer clubs.\n227\t  - Clubs are 25, 50, 100, 250, 500 or 1000. Counts are 1-999.\n228\t  - At most 10 entries. Each club and kind appears at most once.\n229\t  - Each refusal names the bad entry: \"milestones: 'R30' is not a club (25,\n230\t    50, 100, 250, 500, 1000)\"; \"milestones: R25 appears twice\"; \"milestones:\n231\t    11 entries, at most 10 fit one card\".\n232\t- **`date`**: `YYYY-MM-DD` and a real calendar date. The weekday is computed\n233\t  from the date (Zeller or day count), never from a clock. Any weekday is\n234\t  accepted, because junior events and specials run on other days.\n235\t- **Character set**: `eventName` and `footer` accept printable ASCII plus\n236\t  Latin-1 and Latin Extended-A (U+00C0-U+017F, the `DRAWN` set the swim,\n237\t  cubing and radio cards use). Anything else is refused, naming the\n238\t  character.\n239\t- **Fit ladder**:\n240\t  - Event name: shrink to 70% of its design size, then refuse.\n241\t  - Footer: shrink alone to the floor, then refuse.\n242\t  - Never ellipsis.\n243\t  - The floor is `max(6, round(S * 0.022))`. Defaults must clear it on all\n244\t    seven contract canvases.\n245\t- **`accent`**: `isColor` plus `colorPicker`, validated `#rrggbb`, with `\"\"`\n246\t  falling back to the default. Hero numbers in the accent must keep 4.5:1\n247\t  contrast against the page. If the user's accent fails that, the numbers go\n248\t  to ink and only fills use the accent.\n249\t- **Page**: light paper (`#f6f4ee`) and ink (`#1b1f1c`). It prints, and it\n250\t  reads on Facebook's light and dark themes because the card is its own\n251\t  rectangle.\n252\t\n253\tTest vectors:\n254\t\n255\t| input | expected |\n256\t|---|---|\n257\t| `4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25` | badges 25 `4 runners`, 50 `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`, 25 `2 volunteers` (volunteer fill) |\n258\t| `1xr100,4xR25` | 25 `4 runners`, then 100 `1 runner` |\n259\t| `\"\"` | no badges; line `No milestone clubs this week` |\n260\t| `4xR30` | refused, names `R30` |\n261\t| `4xR25, 2xR25` | refused, duplicate |\n262\t| 6 entries | two rows, 3 + 3 |\n263\t| 10 entries | two rows, 5 + 5 |\n264\t| 11 entries | refused |\n265\t| `counts.finishers 1204` | `1,204` |\n266\t| `date \"2026-10-03\"` | `SAT 03 OCT 2026` |\n267\t| `date \"2026-02-30\"` | refused |\n268\t\n269\tStress copy for the sweep:\n270\t\n271\t- `eventName \"Great Salterns Nature Reserve 5k\"` (32 characters) and a\n272\t  40-character name.\n273\t- All counts at 9999 (`9,999`).\n274\t- 10 badges.\n275\t- A 70-character footer.\n276\t\n277\t## Beats\n278\t\n279\tNone; it is a still. No intro animation: the frame is the finished card.\n280\t\n281\t## Defaults must show\n282\t\n283\tAt 1080x1080, with no inputs, a stranger sees:\n284\t\n285\t- The header `WILLOWMERE PARK 5K` with `#312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026` under it,\n286\t  and an accent rule.\n287\t- Two big tiles: `214` / `finishers` and `31` / `volunteers`.\n288\t- Four smaller tiles: `38` / `new PBs`, `27` / `first timers`, `19` /\n289\t  `visitors`, `4` / `first-time volunteers`.\n290\t- The band `MILESTONE CLUBS` with four badges: 25 `4 runners`, 50\n291\t  `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`, then a neutral 25 `2 volunteers`.\n292\t- The footer `Sample week: event and numbers are invented`.\n293\t\n294\tAll of it is ASCII. Nothing says \"parkrun\", yet a run director knows the\n295\tlayout at a glance: these are their results-page numbers in their order.\n296\t\n297\tHonest weakness the defaults will show: at 480x270 the stat labels are near\n298\tthe floor (about 7-8 px), and that canvas is a thumbnail.\n299\t\n300\t## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n301\t\n302\t1. **The week reads in two seconds.** The two hero numbers are clearly the\n303\t   largest text on the card at every canvas (at least 1.5x the stat values).\n304\t   A viewer can say \"214 ran, 31 volunteered\" before reading anything else.\n305\t   The four supporting tiles read as one row or grid of equals.\n306\t2. **Every number is exactly what was typed.** Six counts, run number, date\n307\t   and badge counts appear exactly as given, with `1,204` style commas and a\n308\t   correct weekday. There are no invented derived stats, no `k` and no\n309\t   malformed digits. Every bad input is refused with a message that names\n310\t   the field and the value: unknown counts key, missing key, PBs above\n311\t   finishers, bad club, duplicate club, 11 badges, bad date.\n312\t3. **The milestone band holds in every week.** It works with 0, 1, 4, 6 and\n313\t   10 badges at 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1920x1080. The empty week shows the\n314\t   one line and keeps the band. Badges are equal, centred and ordered run\n315\t   then volunteer, ascending. Run and volunteer badges differ by caption word\n316\t   as well as fill.\n317\t4. **Balanced at all three aspects.** There is no band of dead air bigger\n318\t   than one gap plus one tile row at 1080x1920 or 1920x1080. No tile is a\n319\t   slab (taller than about 1.3x its width). Text fits everywhere, with no\n320\t   refusal at defaults on the seven contract canvases. Labels are one shared\n321\t   size.\n322\t5. **It is the RD's card, not ours.** It has no parkrun word, logo or\n323\t   palette, and no template credit. The `footer` sample line goes away with\n324\t   `\"\"`, and the space goes back into the layout. The props mirror the\n325\t   runstats field names closely enough to fill from that list in a minute.\n326\t   The registry description says the numbers are typed in, not fetched.\n327\t\n328\t## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n329\t\n330\t- **a (baseline):** as specified, with the two hero tiles, light paper and\n331\t  the green accent.\n332\t- **b (layout: six equals):** no hero row. All six counts are equal tiles in\n333\t  a qsl-style reflow: 3x2 wide and square, 2x3 portrait. Everything else is\n334\t  unchanged. This tests whether the hierarchy earns its space.\n335\t- **c (palette: dark page):** night paper (`#14211a`) with light ink and the\n336\t  same accent family (lightened to keep 4.5:1). Badges are tuned for dark. It\n337\t  is for event pages whose feed is photo-heavy, where a dark card stands out.\n338\t  This is one palette change, not a `preset` prop.\n339\t\n340\tLeave the one intended to ship last in place, with its choices as the\n341\tdefaults. The tests and WHY must follow that variant's `DEFAULTS`: swim b\n342\tdied on a WHY that described a.\n343\t\n344\t## What is weak in this plan\n345\t\n346\t- The demand is one Chrome extension's README and two text tools. I have\n347\t  not seen a PowerPoint original (the Rushmoor and Great Salterns pages were\n348\t  not opened). The tile set mirrors the tools, not a seen design.\n349\t- There is no importer. The RD retypes six numbers and a milestones line\n350\t  each week. The `milestones` syntax is runstats' syntax, but `counts` is\n351\t  JSON, which is friction for a volunteer in a hurry.\n352\t- The `V` prefix for volunteer clubs is my extension; runstats prints run\n353\t  milestones only.\n354\t- Without the trademark, the card looks like any 5k's weekly summary. That\n355\t  makes it reusable, but a little anonymous at defaults.\n356\t- 480x270 is a thumbnail. The labels there will be near the floor.\n357\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a","uuid":"fa2b44f9-587a-4aa9-b479-c56126dd7796","timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:10:25.888Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-06\\20-brief.md","content":"# Brief — 2026-10-06\n\n## The use case (two sentences, from the scout)\n\nEvery Saturday a free, timed, volunteer-run 5k (parkrun, in 20+ countries)\ngets the same numbers: finishers, new PBs, first timers, visitors, volunteers\nand the milestone clubs reached. The run director or report writer turns them\ninto \"this week at our event\" for the Facebook page and the results/news\npage, today by hand in PowerPoint\n([ear1grey/parkrun-event-summary](https://github.com/ear1grey/parkrun-event-summary):\n\"quite cumbersome\") or as plain text\n([eventuate](https://github.com/johnsyweb/eventuate),\n[parkrun-runstats](https://github.com/rwkura/parkrun-milestones)).\n\n## Neighbours read\n\nPlan call 1 ran four readers and was cut off. The three digests that finished\nare in [`plan-notes/`](plan-notes/): docs, neighbours, official shapes. The\nparkrun facts reader did not finish, so the domain facts below come from the\nscout.\n\n- `community/qsl-card/v1`: a fixed 6-cell table that reflows by aspect, with a\n  pure layout function placed by `placeInsetPieces`. Reflowing comes first and\n  shrinking is the second resort. Its lesson: chrome you cannot remove\n  (`ADIF QSO CARD`) is a defect.\n- `music/radio-top-30-chart/v1`: the `w*10 >= h*13` wide switch and invented\n  sample data labelled in the footer. Its lesson: about 30 tile and text\n  layers tripped `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP`, and the dim ink was invisible in a feed.\n- `sports/cubing-average-card/v1` and `sports/swim-time-drop-card/v1`: in\n  portrait, extra height turned into dead air. Tiles capped against becoming\n  slabs left half a square empty.\n- Official `hero/ffmpeg-pulse/kpi-overview/v1` and `github/year-card/v1`: a KPI\n  grid of 4x2 / 3 / 2 columns by aspect, each tile a big number over a small\n  label (value about 0.42-0.5 of tile height, label about 0.16-0.2).\n\nWhat is new against those: no card on the shelf is a group's week. This one\nhas a hierarchy across tiles (two headline numbers over four supporting ones)\nand a variable badge row (0 to 10 milestone clubs) that needs an empty-week\nrule.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1`. The pack exists: \"Cards a\n  hobby community makes for its own members, filled from the records the hobby\n  already keeps\". A weekly card made by event volunteers from the results page\n  fits it word for word. `sports` holds only one athlete's PB cards.\n- title: Weekly 5k Run Report\n- kind: image (still PNG). Canvas hint 1080x1080 (the Facebook feed square).\n  It must also work at 1920x1080 (results page, slide), 1080x1920 (story) and\n  the seven contract canvases, down to 480x270, with no refusal at defaults.\n- duration: still (`outputHints` `{ width: 1080, height: 1080, fps: 30,\n  durationMs: 2000, format: { kind: \"image\", container: \"png\" }, note }`)\n\n## The design decisions\n\n1. **Two headline numbers, not six equal ones.** Finishers and volunteers get\n   the two big tiles, side by side and the same size. An event has no run\n   without either, and the run report thanks both. New PBs, first timers,\n   visitors and first-time volunteers sit under them as four smaller tiles.\n   Six equal tiles is variant b, so the critic can compare.\n2. **Numbers are props, never fetched, never computed.** The card prints what\n   the RD types. It derives no percentages, no \"record week\" and no ranking.\n   The only computation is formatting (thousands comma) and the weekday from\n   the date.\n3. **The milestone band never moves.** With no milestones, the band stays and\n   holds one line, \"No milestone clubs this week\". The card keeps the same\n   shape every Saturday, which matters for a weekly series. More than 5 clubs\n   wrap to two rows inside the same band.\n4. **No parkrun marks.** The title, the defaults and the labels never use the\n   word \"parkrun\", a logo, or the purple/apricot palette. The user's own\n   `eventName` may say \"Rushmoor parkrun\"; that is their copy. Labels use\n   plain words: \"finishers\", \"volunteers\", \"first timers\".\n5. **Labels are fixed copy, broken in advance.** \"first-time volunteers\" is\n   the long label and sets the tile label size. It is written as two lines,\n   `first-time` / `volunteers`, so a 4-wide row fits at 480x270. All tile\n   labels share one size (the minimum across tiles), as qsl-card does.\n6. **Any mark is a prop.** The only free line is `footer`, and `\"\"` removes\n   it. The template prints no credit and no pitch of its own.\n\n## Layout\n\nMargin `m = 0.05 * S`, gap `0.025 * S`, with `S = min(H, 0.75 * W)`. Bands\nare fractions of the content height, given as targets, not pins. The wide\nswitch is `W * 10 >= H * 13`, as in the radio and cubing cards. Place every\nregion as a real rect with `placeInsetPieces` from a pure layout function, the\nqsl-card shape. There are no full-canvas sources and no `size` exprs. Text is\nstatic svg text in the bundled font, over a `makeColorTile` where there is a\nfill. The page colour goes in `document.backgroundColor`.\n\nSquare and portrait (stacked), at 1080x1080:\n\n```\n+--------------------------------------------+\n| WILLOWMERE PARK 5K                         |  header ~15%\n| #312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026                   |\n+---------------------+----------------------+\n|        214          |         31           |  hero row ~28%\n|     finishers       |      volunteers      |  (2 equal tiles)\n+----------+----------+----------+-----------+\n|   38     |   27     |   19     |    4      |  stat row ~20%\n| new PBs  | first    | visitors | first-time|  (4 equal tiles;\n|          | timers   |          | volunteers|   2x2 when portrait)\n+----------+----------+----------+-----------+\n| MILESTONE CLUBS                            |  milestone band ~25%\n|  [25] [50] [100] [25]                      |\n|  4 runners 3 runners 1 runner 2 volunteers |\n+--------------------------------------------+\n| Sample week: event and numbers are invented|  footer ~5%\n+--------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n- Square (`0.8 <= W/H < 1.3`) puts the four stat tiles in one 4x1 row.\n- Portrait (`W/H < 0.8`) makes the stat grid 2x2, and the bands grow with H\n  (hero about 26%, stats about 26%). Values are capped by width as well as\n  height, so 1080x1920 gets bigger numbers instead of dead air. Cap tile\n  heights so a tile is never taller than about 1.3x its width. Put the slack\n  between bands as equal gaps, not under the footer.\n\nWide (`W * 10 >= H * 13`), at 1920x1080:\n\n```\n+------------------------------------------------------------+\n| WILLOWMERE PARK 5K                 #312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026 |  header ~16%\n+-------------------+----------------------------------------+\n|       214         |    38 new PBs     |   27 first timers   |\n|    finishers      |-------------------+---------------------|  middle ~52%\n|-------------------|    19 visitors    |  4 first-time vols  |\n|        31         |                   |  (two lines)        |\n|    volunteers     |                   |                     |\n+-------------------+-------------------+---------------------+\n| MILESTONE CLUBS  [25] [50] [100] [25]                       |  band ~24%\n| Sample week: event and numbers are invented                 |  footer ~5%\n+------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n- The left column is about 36% of the width and holds the two hero tiles\n  stacked. The right is a 2x2 stat grid.\n- The run number and date move to the right end of the header line. If the\n  line does not fit, they drop to a second line, the same as square.\n\nMilestone badges:\n\n- A badge is a rounded tile (`roundedRectMask`, or the `effects.rounding` of\n  `makeColorTile`) with the club number big and a caption below:\n  `4 runners` / `1 runner` / `2 volunteers` / `1 volunteer`.\n- Run clubs fill with the accent. Volunteer clubs fill with a neutral\n  (light: a tinted grey; ink flips with `onColor`), so the two kinds differ by\n  fill AND by caption word, never by colour alone.\n- Order: run clubs ascending, then volunteer clubs ascending.\n- All badges are the same size. At most 5 per row: 6-10 badges make two rows\n  of `ceil(n/2)` and `floor(n/2)`. A row narrower than the band is centred.\n\nOverlay depth: about 6 tiles x 3 layers, 10 badges x 3 and the header and\nfooter come to near 50 sources. Keep each text in its own tile's cell, as a\n2-layer stack (fill plus text), never a full-canvas chain. Check the CLI for\n`OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` at 10 badges, and use child documents per band if it\nfires (the powerlifting fix).\n\n## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps)\n\nLabels are the build's to name; these are the promises.\n\n- Every text fits its box (`textFitsMeasured`, budget `cell * 0.94 - 2px`).\n  That covers event name, run line, each value, each label line, the band\n  title, each badge number and caption, the empty-week line and the footer.\n  Use one label per field and tile, since the copy differs.\n- Header at the top: event name `within yFrac [0, 0.25]`.\n- Footer at the bottom when present: `within yFrac [0.9, 1]`.\n- Hero tiles: exactly 2, `equal: \"size\"` (tolerancePx 2), each\n  `within yFrac [0.1, 0.8]`.\n- Stat tiles: exactly 4, `equal: \"size\"` (tolerancePx 2), each\n  `minWidthFrac 0.15`.\n- Milestone band: `within yFrac [0.55, 1]`, `minWidthFrac 0.85`. It is\n  present every week. Badges are `equal: \"size\"` when there are 2 or more,\n  each `within` the band's y range. With 0 badges the contract declares the\n  empty-week line instead of the badge label, so there is no `missing-label`\n  and no `too-few`.\n- Presence: a value and a label for all six counts; one badge per milestone\n  entry.\n- No pinned fractions. The use case does not ask for one.\n\nIn the test, not the contract:\n\n- The hero value px is at least 1.5x the stat value px, at every contract\n  canvas.\n- All tile labels share one px size.\n- Badge order and captions are as listed in the test vectors.\n- Determinism, and each validation error by message.\n- A grep over the defaults and labels finds no \"parkrun\".\n\n## Props (name · type · default · what it changes · required?)\n\n| # | prop | type | default | what it changes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `eventName` | string | `\"Willowmere Park 5k\"` | Header title, drawn in caps. Up to 40 characters. |\n| 2 | `runNumber` | number | `312` | `#312` in the run line. Integer 1-9999. |\n| 3 | `date` | string | `\"2026-10-03\"` | `SAT 03 OCT 2026` in the run line. `\"\"` drops the date and its separator. |\n| 4 | `counts` | json | `{\"finishers\":214,\"newPbs\":38,\"firstTimers\":27,\"visitors\":19,\"volunteers\":31,\"firstTimeVolunteers\":4}` | The six tiles. |\n| 5 | `milestones` | string | `\"4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25\"` | The badges. `\"\"` shows the empty-week line. |\n| 6 | `footer` | string | `\"Sample week: event and numbers are invented\"` | The bottom line. `\"\"` removes it, and the slack goes to the gaps. |\n| 7 | `accent` | string (colour) | `\"#1f7a4d\"` | Run-club badge fill, the header rule and the hero numbers. |\n| 8 | `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | Draws the layout-intent overlay. |\n\nAll props are optional and every default renders a full card.\n\nRules, not props:\n\n- **`counts`**:\n  - It must hold exactly the six keys above, each an integer >= 0.\n    `finishers` must be >= 1.\n  - An unknown key is refused by name (\"counts: unknown key 'pb'; use\n    finishers, newPbs, ...\"), because a silently ignored key is the QSL lesson.\n  - A missing key is refused by name. An invented default never fills a real\n    week.\n  - Sanity checks:\n    - `newPbs`, `firstTimers` and `visitors` are each <= `finishers`.\n    - `firstTimeVolunteers` <= `volunteers`.\n    - Values go up to 9999.\n  - Each field is bound with `bindPropPath(cell, \"counts\", [key], \"number\")`.\n- **Number format**: a thousands comma from 1000 up (`1204` -> `1,204`). Use\n  ASCII digits, and no \"k\" abbreviation; the RD wants the exact count.\n- **`milestones`**:\n  - Comma-separated entries `<count>x<R|V><club>`, case-insensitive, with\n    whitespace tolerated. This is the\n    [parkrun-runstats](https://github.com/rwkura/parkrun-milestones) line\n    (`4xR25, 4xR50, 1xR100`) plus `V` for volunteer clubs.\n  - Clubs are 25, 50, 100, 250, 500 or 1000. Counts are 1-999.\n  - At most 10 entries. Each club and kind appears at most once.\n  - Each refusal names the bad entry: \"milestones: 'R30' is not a club (25,\n    50, 100, 250, 500, 1000)\"; \"milestones: R25 appears twice\"; \"milestones:\n    11 entries, at most 10 fit one card\".\n- **`date`**: `YYYY-MM-DD` and a real calendar date. The weekday is computed\n  from the date (Zeller or day count), never from a clock. Any weekday is\n  accepted, because junior events and specials run on other days.\n- **Character set**: `eventName` and `footer` accept printable ASCII plus\n  Latin-1 and Latin Extended-A (U+00C0-U+017F, the `DRAWN` set the swim,\n  cubing and radio cards use). Anything else is refused, naming the\n  character.\n- **Fit ladder**:\n  - Event name: shrink to 70% of its design size, then refuse.\n  - Footer: shrink alone to the floor, then refuse.\n  - Never ellipsis.\n  - The floor is `max(6, round(S * 0.022))`. Defaults must clear it on all\n    seven contract canvases.\n- **`accent`**: `isColor` plus `colorPicker`, validated `#rrggbb`, with `\"\"`\n  falling back to the default. Hero numbers in the accent must keep 4.5:1\n  contrast against the page. If the user's accent fails that, the numbers go\n  to ink and only fills use the accent.\n- **Page**: light paper (`#f6f4ee`) and ink (`#1b1f1c`). It prints, and it\n  reads on Facebook's light and dark themes because the card is its own\n  rectangle.\n\nTest vectors:\n\n| input | expected |\n|---|---|\n| `4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25` | badges 25 `4 runners`, 50 `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`, 25 `2 volunteers` (volunteer fill) |\n| `1xr100,4xR25` | 25 `4 runners`, then 100 `1 runner` |\n| `\"\"` | no badges; line `No milestone clubs this week` |\n| `4xR30` | refused, names `R30` |\n| `4xR25, 2xR25` | refused, duplicate |\n| 6 entries | two rows, 3 + 3 |\n| 10 entries | two rows, 5 + 5 |\n| 11 entries | refused |\n| `counts.finishers 1204` | `1,204` |\n| `date \"2026-10-03\"` | `SAT 03 OCT 2026` |\n| `date \"2026-02-30\"` | refused |\n\nStress copy for the sweep:\n\n- `eventName \"Great Salterns Nature Reserve 5k\"` (32 characters) and a\n  40-character name.\n- All counts at 9999 (`9,999`).\n- 10 badges.\n- A 70-character footer.\n\n## Beats\n\nNone; it is a still. No intro animation: the frame is the finished card.\n\n## Defaults must show\n\nAt 1080x1080, with no inputs, a stranger sees:\n\n- The header `WILLOWMERE PARK 5K` with `#312  |  SAT 03 OCT 2026` under it,\n  and an accent rule.\n- Two big tiles: `214` / `finishers` and `31` / `volunteers`.\n- Four smaller tiles: `38` / `new PBs`, `27` / `first timers`, `19` /\n  `visitors`, `4` / `first-time volunteers`.\n- The band `MILESTONE CLUBS` with four badges: 25 `4 runners`, 50\n  `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`, then a neutral 25 `2 volunteers`.\n- The footer `Sample week: event and numbers are invented`.\n\nAll of it is ASCII. Nothing says \"parkrun\", yet a run director knows the\nlayout at a glance: these are their results-page numbers in their order.\n\nHonest weakness the defaults will show: at 480x270 the stat labels are near\nthe floor (about 7-8 px), and that canvas is a thumbnail.\n\n## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n\n1. **The week reads in two seconds.** The two hero numbers are clearly the\n   largest text on the card at every canvas (at least 1.5x the stat values).\n   A viewer can say \"214 ran, 31 volunteered\" before reading anything else.\n   The four supporting tiles read as one row or grid of equals.\n2. **Every number is exactly what was typed.** Six counts, run number, date\n   and badge counts appear exactly as given, with `1,204` style commas and a\n   correct weekday. There are no invented derived stats, no `k` and no\n   malformed digits. Every bad input is refused with a message that names\n   the field and the value: unknown counts key, missing key, PBs above\n   finishers, bad club, duplicate club, 11 badges, bad date.\n3. **The milestone band holds in every week.** It works with 0, 1, 4, 6 and\n   10 badges at 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1920x1080. The empty week shows the\n   one line and keeps the band. Badges are equal, centred and ordered run\n   then volunteer, ascending. Run and volunteer badges differ by caption word\n   as well as fill.\n4. **Balanced at all three aspects.** There is no band of dead air bigger\n   than one gap plus one tile row at 1080x1920 or 1920x1080. No tile is a\n   slab (taller than about 1.3x its width). Text fits everywhere, with no\n   refusal at defaults on the seven contract canvases. Labels are one shared\n   size.\n5. **It is the RD's card, not ours.** It has no parkrun word, logo or\n   palette, and no template credit. The `footer` sample line goes away with\n   `\"\"`, and the space goes back into the layout. The props mirror the\n   runstats field names closely enough to fill from that list in a minute.\n   The registry description says the numbers are typed in, not fetched.\n\n## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n\n- **a (baseline):** as specified, with the two hero tiles, light paper and\n  the green accent.\n- **b (layout: six equals):** no hero row. All six counts are equal tiles in\n  a qsl-style reflow: 3x2 wide and square, 2x3 portrait. Everything else is\n  unchanged. This tests whether the hierarchy earns its space.\n- **c (palette: dark page):** night paper (`#14211a`) with light ink and the\n  same accent family (lightened to keep 4.5:1). Badges are tuned for dark. It\n  is for event pages whose feed is photo-heavy, where a dark card stands out.\n  This is one palette change, not a `preset` prop.\n\nLeave the one intended to ship last in place, with its choices as the\ndefaults. The tests and WHY must follow that variant's `DEFAULTS`: swim b\ndied on a WHY that described a.\n\n## What is weak in this plan\n\n- The demand is one Chrome extension's README and two text tools. I have\n  not seen a PowerPoint original (the Rushmoor and Great Salterns pages were\n  not opened). The tile set mirrors the tools, not a seen design.\n- There is no importer. The RD retypes six numbers and a milestones line\n  each week. The `milestones` syntax is runstats' syntax, but `counts` is\n  JSON, which is friction for a volunteer in a hurry.\n- The `V` prefix for volunteer clubs is my extension; runstats prints run\n  milestones only.\n- Without the trademark, the card looks like any 5k's weekly summary. That\n  makes it reusable, but a little anonymous at defaults.\n- 480x270 is a thumbnail. The labels there will be near the floor.\n","numLines":357,"startLine":1,"totalLines":357}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmGvhy7ANTvXJWdhnD3s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016g1xgMWJLAHCar6h1iuoDx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-06\\10-scout.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":34886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a","uuid":"270d5c7b-ad18-4707-90f0-daa5f8f016a2","timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:10:26.409Z","request_id":"req_011CfmGvhfzYmuCKJYQdP1vZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016g1xgMWJLAHCar6h1iuoDx":{"file_path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-06\\10-scout.md"}}}
