ng up to half a gap to reach\n  a lattice line. A test pins it: no child ref carries an inset, and every\n  child canvas is 5-smooth.\n- **A still's child is encoded 4:2:0 with no alpha.** Rounded tile corners\n  showed the child's own cream a shade off the page (a `black@0` base renders\n  black). Pure white clipped into a grey 16x16 block in each corner, and a\n  warm off-white lost its tint at the right edge. What worked: square tiles,\n  and a neutral `#fbfbfb` fill that comes out flat at 251,251,251.\n\n## Departures from the brief (on purpose)\n\n- Event name: one line down to 70% of its size, then two lines, then smaller\n  down to the floor. The brief says refuse after 70%, but it also lists a\n  40-character name as stress copy that must render.\n- Ten clubs: on a wide band the card may use one row of n when that draws the\n  badges larger (it chose two rows at 1920x1080). Ten clubs refuse at 640x360\n  and 480x270. Badge copy has its own floor of `max(6, 1.4% of S)` (15 px at\n  1080), below the page floor.\n- Tiles are square-cornered and near-white (see above). Tiles snap to the\n  lattice, so their edges can sit 3-6 px inside the band edges (visible on\n  the square's stat row).\n\n## In place now: a\n\n`src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/` is byte-identical to\n`variants/a/src/`, and the registry row carries a's description. Scratch\n(edit scripts, `probe.cjs`, `scratch/`) is under `journal/2026-10-06/`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":423392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a","uuid":"caedbdbb-571e-4233-aea2-3747d1c7b790"