2)","+`src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/` (scaffolded by `npm run new`), registry","+row in `src/community/registry.ts`. A still PNG, hinted at 1080x1080. A pure","+`layoutWeeklyRunReport` (the qsl-card shape) places every rect; `render` turns","+them into pieces. 14 unit tests: the default strings, bindings (six","+`bindPropPath` counts plus the header props, footer, accent and band), the","+layout sweep at the seven contract canvases for 13 prop sets, hierarchy and","+one label size at every canvas, reflow, the milestone band (0 / 6 / 10 clubs),","+the runstats parser, number and date formats, every refusal by message, the","+no-\"parkrun\" grep, determinism, and the child-document rule below."," ","-- Scaffolded `@one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1` (state.scaffolded = true).","-- Template, registry row, WHY and 14 unit tests written; `npm run build` clean,","-  jest 14/14, fingerprint written, `variants/a` rendered (exit 0 x3 + tutorial),","-  0 `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` in the three `renders/*.output.json`.","-- Fixed: every default render warned `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` 26-27 deep (45 with ten","-  clubs) - text over a tile fill never lowers onto the grid sheet. Now each tile","-  and each badge is a CHILD document (`settleLayout` finds the parent lattice","-  pitch, `snapGroup` puts tiles/badges on it with 5-smooth sides, parent basis","-  360). Stress renders in `variants/a/extra/` show no chain warning anywhere.","-  Why the snapping: the layout checker inlines a child into its lattice cell and","-  ignores the ref's inset (tiles judged 152-160 px when the engine drew 150), and","-  `latticeSmooth` checks child canvases.","-- Fixed: tile corners are square now. A still's child has no alpha (a `black@0`","-  base renders black) and a child's cream encodes a shade lighter than the page,","-  so a rounded tile corner showed a ghost (`scratch/corner*.png`). Badges stay","-  rounded on the white band (white matches white).","-- Re-opened portrait after the square-corner change: tiles square, all strings right, but a 16x16 block at the top-left of each tile child is a shade off white (#fbfbfb-ish vs #fff; `scratch/corner-sq.png`) - looks like the child intermediate encode (one macroblock). Ideas: an off-white tile fill so the block cannot show, or check whether badge children show it too; and the hero->stats gap is ~56 px vs ~24 elsewhere.","-- OPEN: snapping slack shows as uneven gaps in portrait (hero->stats gap ~56 px","-  vs 20). Distribute slack evenly or snap the band heights before positions.","-- Then: variants b (six equal tiles) and c (dark page), per the brief.","-- Scratch: `probe.cjs` (px per canvas via settleLayout), `scratch-measure.cjs`,","-  `scratch-*.cjs` (one-off edit scripts), `scratch/`.","-- Pixel check (portrait render): tile body 255,255,255, each tile child's","-  top-left 16x16 block 252,252,252; badge body 29,121,76 vs its top-left block","-  29,121,74 (invisible on green). Page is 244,243,236. Decide next call: accept","-  and say so, or try an off-white tile fill.","-- 09:54: TILE is now `#fcfbf8` (off-white). Rendered portrait: tile corner block","-  and body both 250,251,243 - the block is gone. NOT yet rebuilt with the gate,","-  fingerprint not updated, variants/a not re-rendered with it.","+Final gate for the variant in place (a): `npm run build` clean (no warning for","+this template), `npx eslint .` clean, `npm test` 368 jest + 61 node tests","+pass, fingerprint written.","+","+## Variant a — two headline numbers over four smaller tiles, light paper, green accent · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: as promised","+","+The brief's baseline. Renders: landscape, portrait and square exit 0, with","+`\"warnings\": []` in all three `renders/*.output.json`; tutorial exit 0.","+","+Stills, string by string:","+- Header `WILLOWMERE PARK 5K`; `#312 | SAT 03 OCT 2026` under it (to the right","+  on landscape); the accent rule under both.","+- `214 finishers` and `31 volunteers` in green, the largest text on every","+  canvas. Under them `38 new PBs`, `27 first timers`, `19 visitors`,","+  `4 first-time volunteers`: in one row on the square (that label breaks in","+  two), 2x2 in portrait, and a 2x2 grid right of the stacked pair on landscape.","+- `MILESTONE CLUBS` with green 25 `4 runners`, 50 `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`","+  and a grey 25 `2 volunteers`.","+- The footer `Sample week: event and numbers are invented`.","+","+Every claim in the header comment, the `description` and `WHY.solution` is in","+the picture: the hierarchy, the commas, the weekday, the kept band, no","+parkrun word.","+","+Headline / stat number px (ratio), shared label px:","+","+| canvas | headline | stat | ratio | label |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 1080x1080 | 140 | 87 | 1.61 | 22 |","+| 1080x1920 | 211 | 130 | 1.62 | 28 |","+| 1920x1080 | 109 | 68 | 1.60 | 37 |","+| 480x270 | 27 | 16 | 1.69 | 9 |","+","+Stress renders through the CLI, all from the final source","+(`variants/a/extra/`, props in `*.props.json`). All exit 0 with no engine","+warning:","+- `ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows","+  of 5, run clubs then volunteer clubs, each ascending. At 640x360 they are","+  refused: \"milestones cannot be fitted on 640x360 above the 6px readability","+  floor\" (exit 1, `ten-640x360.log`).","+- `empty`: the band stays and says `No milestone clubs this week`; with","+  `footer \"\"` the space goes back to the card.","+- `long`: a 40-character name wraps to two lines in portrait, with `1,204`,","+  `#1043`, six clubs (3 + 3) and a 70-character footer.","+- `maxed`: all counts `9,999`. Defaults at 3840x2160, 640x360 and 480x270.","+","+## Variant b — six equal tiles, no headline pair · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: as promised","+","+One idea changed: all six counts are equal tiles in the runstats order","+(finishers, new PBs, first timers, visitors, volunteers, first-time","+volunteers). They are 3x2 on square and wide, 2x3 in portrait, all ink, one","+number size (122 px on the square, 162 in portrait). The header comment,","+description, WHY solution and tests were rewritten for b, and its snapshot is","+internally true. It reads as a tidy stats board, but \"214 ran, 31","+volunteered\" no longer jumps out: 31 sits mid-grid in row two. Rubric 1","+(headline at least 1.5x the stats) cannot hold by construction.","+","+## Variant c — a's layout on a night page · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: as promised","+","+One palette change on a: page `#14211a`, ink `#eef2ee`, labels `#b4beb7`,","+neutral dark tiles `#2c2c2c`. The accent family is lightened to `#3fae74`","+(5.0:1 on the tiles). Badge text flips to the dark ink on the light green.","+The volunteer badge is `#5a5a5a` with white text. Contrast: labels 7.3:1 on","+the tiles, badge text 6.0-6.9:1. Tiles against the page are only 1.19:1, so","+the cards are quiet. It stands out in a photo feed but does not print.","+","+## Why-tutorial","+","+- Problem page (2/6): who (event teams, run directors, report writers), then","+  ear1grey's PowerPoint quote (\"quite cumbersome\"), Eventuate's \"to celebrate","+  our community on the Facebook page\", runstats' \"list format\", and the four","+  opened sources. Nothing clips.","+- Solution page (3/6): one card per event per week, typed in, never fetched,","+  props mirroring runstats; the decision is that two numbers carry the week","+  and the milestone band never moves. Three honest caveats: no importer, ten","+  clubs need 1280x720, no parkrun marks.","+","+## What was hard","+","+- **Text over a fill never lowers onto the grid sheet.** The first default","+  render was 26-27 overlays deep (45 with ten clubs), past the ~25 where","+  glyph masks silently degrade. The build gate stayed green; only the CLI's","+  `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` showed it. Each tile and badge is now a child","+  document (fill + text, 3-4 deep), and the parent barely overlaps.","+- **Child documents fight the layout contract.** The checker's flatten","+  inlines a child into its lattice-quantized cell and ignores the ref's","+  inset. Equal tiles were judged 152-160 px tall while the engine drew 150.","+  `latticeSmooth` also checks child canvases. So `settleLayout` finds the","+  parent's placement pitch (basis 360) and `snapGroup` puts every tile and","+  badge on that lattice with 5-smooth sides, leaning up to half a gap to reach","+  a lattice line. A test pins it: no child ref carries an inset, and every","+  child canvas is 5-smooth.","+- **A still's child is encoded 4:2:0 with no alpha.** Rounded tile corners","+  showed the child's own cream a shade off the page (a `black@0` base renders","+  black). Pure white clipped into a grey 16x16 block in each corner, and a","+  warm off-white lost its tint at the right edge. What worked: square tiles,","+  and a neutral `#fbfbfb` fill that comes out flat at 251,251,251.","+","+## Departures from the brief (on purpose)","+","+- Event name: one line down to 70% of its size, then two lines, then smaller","+  down to the floor. The brief says refuse after 70%, but it also lists a","+  40-character name as stress copy that must render.","+- Ten clubs: on a wide band the card may use one row of n when that draws the","+  badges larger (it chose two rows at 1920x1080). Ten clubs refuse at 640x360","+  and 480x270. Badge copy has its own floor of `max(6, 1.4% of S)` (15 px at","+  1080), below the page floor.","+- Tiles are square-cornered and near-white (see above). Tiles snap to the","+  lattice, so their edges can sit 3-6 px inside the band edges (visible on","+  the square's stat row).","+","+## In place now: a","+","+`src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/` is byte-identical to","+`variants/a/src/`, and the registry row carries a's description. Scratch","+(edit scripts, `probe.cjs`, `scratch/`) is under `journal/2026-10-06/`."]}],"originalFile":"# Build — 2026-10-06\n\n(in progress - notes for the next build call)\n\n## State at the end of build call 1 (09:52)\n\n- Scaffolded `@one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1` (state.scaffolded = true).\n- Template, registry row, WHY and 14 unit tests written; `npm run build` clean,\n  jest 14/14, fingerprint written, `variants/a` rendered (exit 0 x3 + tutorial),\n  0 `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` in the three `renders/*.output.json`.\n- Fixed: every default render warned `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` 26-27 deep (45 with ten\n  clubs) - text over a tile fill never lowers onto the grid sheet. Now each tile\n  and each badge is a CHILD document (`settleLayout` finds the parent lattice\n  pitch, `snapGroup` puts tiles/badges on it with 5-smooth sides, parent basis\n  360). Stress renders in `variants/a/extra/` show no chain warning anywhere.\n  Why the snapping: the layout checker inlines a child into its lattice cell and\n  ignores the ref's inset (tiles judged 152-160 px when the engine drew 150), and\n  `latticeSmooth` checks child canvases.\n- Fixed: tile corners are square now. A still's child has no alpha (a `black@0`\n  base renders black) and a child's cream encodes a shade lighter than the page,\n  so a rounded tile corner showed a ghost (`scratch/corner*.png`). Badges stay\n  rounded on the white band (white matches white).\n- Re-opened portrait after the square-corner change: tiles square, all strings right, but a 16x16 block at the top-left of each tile child is a shade off white (#fbfbfb-ish vs #fff; `scratch/corner-sq.png`) - looks like the child intermediate encode (one macroblock). Ideas: an off-white tile fill so the block cannot show, or check whether badge children show it too; and the hero->stats gap is ~56 px vs ~24 elsewhere.\n- OPEN: snapping slack shows as uneven gaps in portrait (hero->stats gap ~56 px\n  vs 20). Distribute slack evenly or snap the band heights before positions.\n- Then: variants b (six equal tiles) and c (dark page), per the brief.\n- Scratch: `probe.cjs` (px per canvas via settleLayout), `scratch-measure.cjs`,\n  `scratch-*.cjs` (one-off edit scripts), `scratch/`.\n- Pixel check (portrait render): tile body 255,255,255, each tile child's\n  top-left 16x16 block 252,252,252; badge body 29,121,76 vs its top-left block\n  29,121,74 (invisible on green). Page is 244,243,236. Decide next call: accept\n  and say so, or try an off-white tile fill.\n- 09:54: TILE is now `#fcfbf8` (off-white). Rendered portrait: tile corner block\n  and body both 250,251,243 - the block is gone. NOT yet rebuilt with the gate,\n  fingerprint not updated, variants/a not re-rendered with it.\n","userModified":false}}
