{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmNPAnTXbPRaSoj8s8Gt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U9QxrRe8KoNqUMoQLbdNyY","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'review-weekly-run-report',\n  description: 'Read-only review of today\\'s template (code, brief compliance, stills vs claims), each finding adversarially verified',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Verify' }],\n}\n\nconst CTX = `Repo: C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day (Windows, Git Bash). Today's template: src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts (+ .test.ts beside it), registry row in src/community/registry.ts. The brief is journal/2026-10-06/20-brief.md, the scout is journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md, the build log is journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md. Rendered stills of the variant in place (a): journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/stills/{square,portrait,landscape,tutorial-1..6}.png, stress renders in journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/extra/*.png (props in *.props.json). dist/ is built from the current src (require('./dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js') exports layoutWeeklyRunReport, settleLayout, parseMilestones, parseCounts, formatCount, formatRunDate, normalizeWeeklyRunReport, WeeklyRunReportV1).\nSTRICT RULES: this is READ-ONLY. Do NOT edit, create or delete any file anywhere except scratch files under journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/ . Never run git commands, npm run build, npm run new, fingerprints, or render-variant. You MAY run node one-liners against dist/, npx jest src/community/weekly-run-report, and 'm0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . -w W -h H --props @file -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/<name>.png' (always with -o under that folder). You can view PNG images with the Read tool.\nReport only REAL defects that a careful critic would flag: wrong output, a claim not true in the picture or code, a brief rule broken without being disclosed in 30-build.md, a crash, a validation hole that lets a wrong number reach the card. Do not report style nits. Each finding must have a concrete reproduction (input -> observed vs expected).`\n\nconst FINDINGS = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          title: { type: 'string' },\n          file: { type: 'string' },\n          repro: { type: 'string', description: 'exact input/command and what you observed vs what is expected' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },\n          suggestedFix: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['title', 'file', 'repro', 'severity', 'suggestedFix'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['findings'],\n}\nconst VERDICT = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    real: { type: 'boolean' },\n    evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'what you ran or looked at, and what it showed' },\n  },\n  required: ['real', 'evidence'],\n}\n\nconst DIMENSIONS = [\n  { key: 'code', prompt: `${CTX}\\n\\nYour lens: CODE CORRECTNESS of weekly-run-report.ts. Hunt for bugs: validation holes (counts parsing, milestones regex: leading zeros, whitespace, 0 counts, case, duplicates across case, clubs, >10), date/weekday math (check several known dates), formatCount, the fit ladder (event name one line / two lines / floor), layout math that could produce negative or zero sizes, overlapping cells, text that could exceed its box, the child-document/lattice snapping (settleLayout/snapGroup) at unusual canvases (e.g. 1000x1000, 1366x768, 1200x630, 720x1280, 2000x500, 500x2000), and anything that would throw at a plausible real input. Actually execute probes with node against dist/ to confirm each finding.` },\n  { key: 'brief', prompt: `${CTX}\\n\\nYour lens: BRIEF COMPLIANCE. Read 20-brief.md closely (props table, rules, test vectors, layout contract, rubric) and compare with the code, the tests and the stills. List every promise the brief makes that the template breaks AND that 30-build.md does not disclose as a deliberate departure. Check each test vector from the brief by running it against dist/. Check the props table (names, types, defaults), the refusal messages (do they name the field and value as the brief requires), the contract labels, the footer/empty-week behaviour, the no-parkrun rule, and that the WHY text (problem/solution/caveats/usage) is true for this code.` },\n  { key: 'visual', prompt: `${CTX}\\n\\nYour lens: CLAIMS vs PICTURES. Open (Read) stills/square.png, portrait.png, landscape.png, tutorial-2.png, tutorial-3.png, tutorial-4.png and the stress renders in variants/a/extra/ (ten-*.png, empty-*.png, long-*.png, maxed-*.png, defaults-*.png). Go string by string: every number well-formed, the weekday correct, captions singular/plural right, badge order (run clubs ascending then volunteer clubs ascending), nothing clipped or overlapping, no dead-air band bigger than one gap plus one tile row at 1080x1920 or 1920x1080, no slab tiles. Then check each claim made by the header comment of weekly-run-report.ts, the registry description and WHY.solution/caveats against what the pictures show. Also check 30-build.md's statements about the stills are true.` },\n]\n\nphase('Review')\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  DIMENSIONS,\n  (d) => agent(d.prompt, { label: `review:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (review, d) => parallel((review?.findings ?? []).map((f) => () =>\n    agent(`${CTX}\\n\\nA reviewer (lens: ${d.key}) reported this finding. Try hard to REFUTE it by reproducing it yourself: run the repro, look at the files/pictures. It is real only if you can reproduce the defect and it is not already disclosed as a deliberate departure in journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md. Default to real=false if you cannot reproduce it.\\n\\nFINDING: ${JSON.stringify(f)}`, { label: `verify:${d.key}:${f.title.slice(0, 40)}`, phase: