{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xiu2rXrhCWKFLavUPnM1r","type":"tool_result","content":"started review:code\nstarted review:brief\nstarted review:visual\nRESULT v2:51485f052 findings 6\n [0] high A misspelled top-level prop silently puts the sample week's invented numbers on a real card, which is the exact failure the header comment says the template prevents \n    repro: I rendered `m0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.props.json -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.png`. The props are {\"eventName\":\"Riverside 5k\",\"runNumber\":88,\"date\":\"2026-10-10\",\"count\":{\"finishers\":120,...},\"milestone\":\"1xR50\",\"footer\":\"Thank you to all our volunteers\"}, so `count` and `milestone` are misspelled.\n\nWhat happens: exit 0 with no warning. The card reads RIVERSIDE 5K #88 SAT 10  \n    fix: In normalizeWeeklyRunReport, refuse any top-level key not in the schema, naming it (e.g. \"unknown prop 'count'; did you mean 'counts'?\"). Also refuse a counts or milestones that falls back to DEFAULTS when eventName or runNumber differs from the sample, or have the header comment and WHY admit that \n [1] medium Following the tutorial's own week.json prints run #313 with the sample week's date and the 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' footer \n    repro: WHY.usage.try[0] (line 687, shown on tutorial-4.png) suggests week.json: {\"eventName\":\"Your Park 5k\",\"runNumber\":313,\"counts\":{...},\"milestones\":\"2xR25, 1xV50\"}. I filled in counts (journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.props.json) and rendered at 1080x1080 to journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.png.\n\nWhat the card shows: '#313 | SAT 03 OCT 2026', which is the default date of sample run #312, a week too early. The footer says 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' un \n    fix: Add \"date\":\"2026-10-10\" and \"footer\":\"\" (or a real thank-you line) to the WHY.usage week.json example. Better still, stop defaulting date when the other props are the user's own: refuse it, or treat it like counts.\n [2] medium Milestone badge counts are never checked against finishers or volunteers, so impossible club numbers reach the card \n    repro: normalizeWeeklyRunReport({counts:{finishers:40,newPbs:5,firstTimers:3,visitors:2,volunteers:8,firstTimeVolunteers:1}, milestones:'90xR25, 30xV25'}) is accepted. It draws badges '25 / 90 runners' and '25 / 30 volunteers' on a week with 40 finishers and 8 volunteers.\n\nWhy that is impossible: every runner who reached a run club this week finished this week, and every volunteer-club member volunteered this week. So the sum of R counts must be at most finishers, and the sum of V counts at most volunt \n    fix: After parsing milestones in normalizeWeeklyRunReport, refuse when sum(R counts) > counts.finishers or sum(V counts) > counts.volunteers. Name the field and both numbers, e.g. \"milestones: 90 runners reached a club but only 40 finished\".\n [3] low 30-build.md describes the ten and long stress renders as two rows (5+5, 3+3), but the wide renders draw a single row \n    repro: 30-build.md lines 51-52 say: '`ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows of 5'. But variants/a/extra/ten-1280x720.png shows all ten badges in ONE row. settleLayout({milestones: ten.props.json milestones}, 1280, 720) confirms it: every badge has rect.y = 528 (badgePx 26, captionPx 11).\n\nLine 57 says '`long`: ... six clubs (3 + 3)'. But extra/long-1920x1080.png shows the six badges in one row of 6; only the 1080x1080 and 1080x1920 renders are 3+3.\n\nThe brief says 'At \n    fix: Correct the stills bullets: ten at 1280x720 is one row of 10, and long at 1920x1080 is one row of 6. Widen the departure note to say that on wide canvases 6-10 clubs may use one row (as at 1280x720, 3840x2160 and in the six-club case at 1920x1080).\n [4] low Caveat and outputHints say only ten clubs need 1280x720 or larger, but eight and nine clubs are also refused at 480x270 \n    repro: settleLayout({milestones:'1xR25,1xR50,1xR100,1xR250,1xR500,1xR1000,1xV25,1xV50'}, 480, 270) throws 'milestones cannot be fitted on 480x270 above the 6px readability floor'. Nine clubs are refused there too; seven clubs still fit, with captions at 6px.\n\nThe WHY caveat (line 728, shown on tutorial-3.png) says 'ten clubs need 1280x720 or larger and are refused on the 640x360 and 480x270 thumbnails'. The outputHints note (line 747) says 'Ten milestone clubs need 1280x720 or larger.' Both imply that  \n    fix: Change the caveat and the outputHints note to say that 8 or more clubs are refused at 480x270 and 10 at 640x360, or relax the badge sizing so 8-9 clubs fit at 480x270.\n [5] low On every wide canvas the milestone club numbers are drawn larger than the four stat numbers, against 'the hierarchy holds on every canvas' \n    repro: settleLayout({}, W, H) gives badgePx versus statPx of:\n- 1920x1080: 76 vs 68\n- 3840x2160: 153 vs 138\n- 1280x720: 51 vs 45\n- 640x360: 25 vs 22\n- 480x270: 20 vs 16\n\nIn stills/landscape.png the white-on-green badge '25' and '100' are visibly taller than '38', '27' and '19'. The headline numbers are only 1.35-1.44x the badge numbers on these canvases (1.35x at 480x270, 27 vs 20).\n\nThe header comment (lines 20-22) says the stat numbers are capped at 1/1.6 of the headline 'so the hierarchy holds on ev \n    fix: Cap badgePx at statPx (or at floor(heroPx/1.6)) in both arrange() and the post-snap sizing. Otherwise, reword the header comment to limit the 1/1.6 hierarchy to the six tiles.\nstarted verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put\nstarted verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\nstarted verify:visual:Milestone badge counts are never checked\nstarted verify:visual:30-build.md describes the ten and long s\nstarted verify:visual:Caveat and outputHints say only ten club\nstarted verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a","uuid":"1d5cdbad-4b9a-4028-871a-06389d29d0c2","timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:29:54.403Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"started review:code\nstarted review:brief\nstarted review:visual\nRESULT v2:51485f052 findings 6\n [0] high A misspelled top-level prop silently puts the sample week's invented numbers on a real card, which is the exact failure the header comment says the template prevents \n    repro: I rendered `m0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.props.json -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.png`. The props are {\"eventName\":\"Riverside 5k\",\"runNumber\":88,\"date\":\"2026-10-10\",\"count\":{\"finishers\":120,...},\"milestone\":\"1xR50\",\"footer\":\"Thank you to all our volunteers\"}, so `count` and `milestone` are misspelled.\n\nWhat happens: exit 0 with no warning. The card reads RIVERSIDE 5K #88 SAT 10  \n    fix: In normalizeWeeklyRunReport, refuse any top-level key not in the schema, naming it (e.g. \"unknown prop 'count'; did you mean 'counts'?\"). Also refuse a counts or milestones that falls back to DEFAULTS when eventName or runNumber differs from the sample, or have the header comment and WHY admit that \n [1] medium Following the tutorial's own week.json prints run #313 with the sample week's date and the 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' footer \n    repro: WHY.usage.try[0] (line 687, shown on tutorial-4.png) suggests week.json: {\"eventName\":\"Your Park 5k\",\"runNumber\":313,\"counts\":{...},\"milestones\":\"2xR25, 1xV50\"}. I filled in counts (journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.props.json) and rendered at 1080x1080 to journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.png.\n\nWhat the card shows: '#313 | SAT 03 OCT 2026', which is the default date of sample run #312, a week too early. The footer says 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' un \n    fix: Add \"date\":\"2026-10-10\" and \"footer\":\"\" (or a real thank-you line) to the WHY.usage week.json example. Better still, stop defaulting date when the other props are the user's own: refuse it, or treat it like counts.\n [2] medium Milestone badge counts are never checked against finishers or volunteers, so impossible club numbers reach the card \n    repro: normalizeWeeklyRunReport({counts:{finishers:40,newPbs:5,firstTimers:3,visitors:2,volunteers:8,firstTimeVolunteers:1}, milestones:'90xR25, 30xV25'}) is accepted. It draws badges '25 / 90 runners' and '25 / 30 volunteers' on a week with 40 finishers and 8 volunteers.\n\nWhy that is impossible: every runner who reached a run club this week finished this week, and every volunteer-club member volunteered this week. So the sum of R counts must be at most finishers, and the sum of V counts at most volunt \n    fix: After parsing milestones in normalizeWeeklyRunReport, refuse when sum(R counts) > counts.finishers or sum(V counts) > counts.volunteers. Name the field and both numbers, e.g. \"milestones: 90 runners reached a club but only 40 finished\".\n [3] low 30-build.md describes the ten and long stress renders as two rows (5+5, 3+3), but the wide renders draw a single row \n    repro: 30-build.md lines 51-52 say: '`ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows of 5'. But variants/a/extra/ten-1280x720.png shows all ten badges in ONE row. settleLayout({milestones: ten.props.json milestones}, 1280, 720) confirms it: every badge has rect.y = 528 (badgePx 26, captionPx 11).\n\nLine 57 says '`long`: ... six clubs (3 + 3)'. But extra/long-1920x1080.png shows the six badges in one row of 6; only the 1080x1080 and 1080x1920 renders are 3+3.\n\nThe brief says 'At \n    fix: Correct the stills bullets: ten at 1280x720 is one row of 10, and long at 1920x1080 is one row of 6. Widen the departure note to say that on wide canvases 6-10 clubs may use one row (as at 1280x720, 3840x2160 and in the six-club case at 1920x1080).\n [4] low Caveat and outputHints say only ten clubs need 1280x720 or larger, but eight and nine clubs are also refused at 480x270 \n    repro: settleLayout({milestones:'1xR25,1xR50,1xR100,1xR250,1xR500,1xR1000,1xV25,1xV50'}, 480, 270) throws 'milestones cannot be fitted on 480x270 above the 6px readability floor'. Nine clubs are refused there too; seven clubs still fit, with captions at 6px.\n\nThe WHY caveat (line 728, shown on tutorial-3.png) says 'ten clubs need 1280x720 or larger and are refused on the 640x360 and 480x270 thumbnails'. The outputHints note (line 747) says 'Ten milestone clubs need 1280x720 or larger.' Both imply that  \n    fix: Change the caveat and the outputHints note to say that 8 or more clubs are refused at 480x270 and 10 at 640x360, or relax the badge sizing so 8-9 clubs fit at 480x270.\n [5] low On every wide canvas the milestone club numbers are drawn larger than the four stat numbers, against 'the hierarchy holds on every canvas' \n    repro: settleLayout({}, W, H) gives badgePx versus statPx of:\n- 1920x1080: 76 vs 68\n- 3840x2160: 153 vs 138\n- 1280x720: 51 vs 45\n- 640x360: 25 vs 22\n- 480x270: 20 vs 16\n\nIn stills/landscape.png the white-on-green badge '25' and '100' are visibly taller than '38', '27' and '19'. The headline numbers are only 1.35-1.44x the badge numbers on these canvases (1.35x at 480x270, 27 vs 20).\n\nThe header comment (lines 20-22) says the stat numbers are capped at 1/1.6 of the headline 'so the hierarchy holds on ev \n    fix: Cap badgePx at statPx (or at floor(heroPx/1.6)) in both arrange() and the post-snap sizing. Otherwise, reword the header comment to limit the 1/1.6 hierarchy to the six tiles.\nstarted verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put\nstarted verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\nstarted verify:visual:Milestone badge counts are never checked\nstarted verify:visual:30-build.md describes the ten and long s\nstarted verify:visual:Caveat and outputHints say only ten club\nstarted verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-06\\logs\\build-1.log","hunks":[{"oldStart":2598,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2598,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_progress\",\"task_id\":\"wnhvgev2n\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01U9QxrRe8KoNqUMoQLbdNyY\",\"description\":\"Verify: verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put\",\"usage\":{\"total_tokens\":566792,\"tool_uses\":142,\"duration_ms\":443626},\"last_tool_name\":\"verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put\",\"summary\":\"Read-only review of today's template (code, brief compliance, stills vs claims), each finding adversarially verified\",\"uuid\":\"07a46233-437a-4326-b6ba-f30a522473da\",\"session_id\":\"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_progress\",\"task_id\":\"wnhvgev2n\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01U9QxrRe8KoNqUMoQLbdNyY\",\"description\":\"Verify: verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\",\"usage\":{\"total_tokens\":566792,\"tool_uses\":143,\"duration_ms\":443770},\"last_tool_name\":\"verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\",\"summary\":\"Read-only review of today's template (code, brief compliance, stills vs claims), each finding adversarially verified\",\"uuid\":\"4c6c76d6-64e6-4cb6-8d17-645c184b2295\",\"session_id\":\"5aa0f356-0a54-4ead-ae70-b6948b14086a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_progress\",\"task_id\":\"wnhvgev2n\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01U9QxrRe8KoNqUMoQLbdNyY\",\"description\":\"Verify: verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club\",\"usage\":{\"total_tokens\":569704,\"tool_uses\":144,\"duration_ms\":444250},\"last_tool_name\":\"verify:visual:On every wide canvas t