{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018heqTLGkMKG3fpW47ju67V","type":"tool_result","content":"REVIEW review:visual 6\nVERDICT verify:visual:30-build.md describes the ten and long s {\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced this. It is a real but low-severity documentation error, and it is narrower than the finding says.\\n\\n1. I ran settleLayout from dist with the props in variants/a/extra/ten.props.json and long.props.json, and counted the d\nVERDICT verify:visual:Caveat and outputHints say only ten club {\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced the finding and the build log does not disclose it.\\n\\n1) I ran a node sweep of settleLayout from dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js with 1 to 10 clubs ('1xR25,...'):\\n   - At 480x270, 1 to 7 clubs wo\nVERDICT verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club {\"real\":false,\"evidence\":\"The measurements are correct, but they don't break any claim or brief rule, so this is not a real defect.\\n\\nWhat I ran: `node` with `settleLayout(props, W, H).L` from dist. With default props it gives hero/stat/badge px of:\\n- 1920x1\nVERDICT verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put {\"real\":false,\"evidence\":\"The behaviour reproduces, but it follows the brief and the repo's conventions, so it is not a defect of this template.\\n\\nWhat I ran: the reviewer's command with journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.props.json (top-level `count` and\nVERDICT verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p {\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced it. The date half is a real defect. The footer half is weaker, because the tutorial's own fourth tip covers it.\\n\\nWhat I ran:\\n1. I rendered `journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.props.json` with m0saic make at\nVERDICT verify:visual:Milestone badge counts are never checked {\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced this in code and in a render. It is not disclosed in 30-build.md.\\n\\n1. Code. Running `node -e` against `dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js`, `normalizeWeeklyRunReport({counts:{finishers:40,newPbs:5,f\nREVIEW review:brief 7\n [0] medium Six milestone clubs render as one row of 6 on every wide canvas: breaks the brief's '6 entries -> 3 + 3' vector and 'at most 5 per row'; 30-build.md discloses this only for ten clubs and says the long set shows 3 + 3 \n    repro: node: settleLayout({milestones:'6xR25, 4xR50, 3xR100, 2xR250, 1xR500, 5xV25'}, W, H).L.badges, rows grouped by rect.y. 1920x1080 gives [6], and so do 1280x720, 3840x2160, 640x360 and 480x270; only 1080x1080 and 1080x1920 give [3,3]. 1920x1080 draws six 216x180 badges in one row. The build's own still journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/extra/long-1920x1080.png shows the six clubs in ONE row, but 30-build.md says '`long`: ... six clubs (3 + 3)'. Expected (brief, Milestone badges and Test vectors): 'At most 5 per row: 6-10 badges make two rows of ceil(n/2) and floor(n/2)' and '6 entries | two rows, 3  \n    fix: Either cap the wide one-row option at 5 (offer arrange([n], n) only when n <= 5, i.e. never for 6-10), or keep the behaviour and fix 30-build.md: make the departure cover 6-10 clubs, not just ten, and correct the 'long ... six clubs (3 + 3)' line to say 3 + 3 on square/portrait and one row of 6 on w\n [1] medium 30-build.md says ten clubs at 1280x720 make 'two rows of 5'; the render and the code put all ten in one row with 11px captions \n    repro: 30-build.md stress section: '`ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows of 5'. journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/extra/ten-1280x720.png shows ONE row of 10 badges. dist agrees: settleLayout({milestones: TEN}, 1280, 720) gives 1 row of 80x80 badges, club 26px, caption 11px (page floor 16). 3840x2160 is also one row of 10. Expected: the claim should match the picture. The brief's test vector is '10 entries | two rows, 5 + 5'. \n    fix: Correct the stress line in 30-build.md: two rows of 5 at 1920x1080, 1080x1080 and 1080x1920; one row of 10 at 1280x720 and 3840x2160, with captions at 11px on 1280x720. Or drop the one-row option so the 5 + 5 claim and the brief's vector both hold.\n [2] medium The WHY 'Use it' example renders a real week with the sample date and the 'event and numbers are invented' footer \n    repro: WHY.usage.try[0] is week.json {\"eventName\":\"Your Park 5k\",\"runNumber\":313,\"counts\":{...},\"milestones\":\"2xR25, 1xV50\"}, with no date and no footer. Rendering it with real counts (m0saic make ... -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/week.json -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/usage-week-313.png) prints '#313 | SAT 03 OCT 2026', which is the invented #312's date, and the footer 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' under the user's real counts. Expected: the brief's 'An invented default never fills a real week' and rubric 2 ('Every number ... date ... appear exact \n    fix: Put \"date\":\"2026-10-10\" and \"footer\":\"\" (or a real thank-you line) in the WHY usage week.json example. Optionally also refuse, or drop the sample footer and date, when counts are supplied but date is left at its default.\n [3] low Milestone counts are not checked against the week's finishers or volunteers, so an impossible badge count reaches the card \n    repro: normalizeWeeklyRunReport({milestones:'999xR25, 500xV25'}) with the default counts (finishers 214, volunteers 31) is ACCEPTED. The card prints '25 / 999 runners' and '25 / 500 volunteers'. Every runner who reaches a run club that week finished that run, and every volunteer-club member volunteered that week. So the run-club counts must sum to at most finishers, and the volunteer-club counts to at most volunteers. A typo like '40xR25' for '4xR25' at a 31-finisher event goes straight onto the public card. The brief only requires counts 1-999, but the header comment's own rationale is 'a silently i \n    fix: In normalizeWeeklyRunReport, after parsing both: sum the R counts and refuse when the sum is greater than counts.finishers ('milestones: 999 runners in run clubs, more than the 214 finishers'); do the same for V counts against counts.volunteers. Add both to the refusal test.\n [4] low footer has a 70-character cap the brief does not set; the brief's fit ladder is 'shrink alone to the floor, then refuse' \n    repro: normalizeWeeklyRunReport({footer: 'Thanks to all 58 volunteers - see you next Saturday at 9am by the cafe!'}) (71 chars) refuses with 'footer \"...\" is 71 characters; the card fits at most 70.' This happens even for a 3840x2160 render, where a 71-character line easily clears the floor. The brief gives eventName a cap ('Up to 40 characters') but none for footer. Its fit ladder says 'Footer: shrink alone to the floor, then refuse'; 70 characters is stress copy, not a limit. The cap (line 286, drawn(p.footer, 'footer', 70, true)) is not listed under 'Departures from the brief' in 30-build.md. \n    fix: Drop the length cap for footer and let the existing fitPx/floor check in layoutWeeklyRunReport refuse per canvas, or list the 70-character cap as a deliberate departure in 30-build.md.\n [5] low 'first-time volunteers' is one line on wide and portrait canvases, against brief decision 5 and the wide mock's '(two lines)'; not listed as a departure \n    repro: layoutWeeklyRunReport({}, W, H).twoLineLabels is false at 1920x1080, 1280x720, 3840x2160, 640x360, 480x270, 1080x1920 and 720x1280; it is true only on square canvases. The stills landscape.png and portrait.png show 'first-time volunteers' on one line. Brief decision 5: 'It is written as two lines, `first-time` / `volunteers`'. The wide layout mock marks the tile '(two lines)'. Code (lines 520-523) uses the two-line form only when the one-line form would cost size. 30-build.md mentions the break only for the square and lists no departure. \n    fix: Either always use TILE_LABEL.firstTimeVolunteers.two, as the brief says, or add the 'one line when it costs n